                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient shows elevated creatinine, suggesting impaired renal function, and mildly decreased total CO₂, which may indicate mild metabolic acidosis. Other parameters, including glucose, urea, electrolytes, and calcium, are within normal limits. Renal function should be further evaluated and correlated clinically.</td>
